🥔 HARVEST ARCHITECTURE WE HAVE ALREADY DECIDED WE NEED

Harvest timing is another important future core requirement.

Each Plant Story should eventually be capable of showing:

expected harvest date/window
likely harvest date/window
actual harvest dates
repeated harvest history

We want Sprig eventually to compare outcomes across the same crop/variety and help reveal anomalies.

For example:

two broccoli plants of the same age behaving differently
potatoes taking much longer in one Growing Place
repeated failures associated with one location
different harvest times from different Growing Recipes

Critically, harvest is crop-dependent.

We do not want one simplistic universal harvest date field.

Examples:

broccoli may have a main head followed by side-shoot harvests
tomatoes produce repeatedly
herbs may be harvested continuously
potatoes tend toward a major harvest
some crops have multiple distinct harvests

The data model eventually needs to respect these patterns.

🧠 LONGER-TERM SPRIG INTELLIGENCE

Sprig is intended eventually to become more than a passive notebook.

Once enough records exist, I want it to help notice patterns in my own garden.

Examples:

"Plants in this Growing Place consistently mature later."
"This Growing Recipe produced better potato yields."
"These two broccoli were planted at the same time but behaved very differently."
"You repeatedly bought this mix at different prices."
"This crop usually takes longer than the packet estimate in your garden."
"Plants in this location struggle during this season."

We are not building an AI engine right now, but please avoid architectural choices that make this future pattern/history analysis impossible.

History matters.

That is one reason purchases, harvests and observations should not simply overwrite previous values.

